r</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Specific effects of depression, panic, and somatic symptoms on illness behavior</article-title><source>Psychosom Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>67</volume><fpage>596</fpage><lpage>601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.psy.0000171158.59706.e7</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Rief W, Martin A, Klaiberg A, Br&#x000e4;hler E. Specific effects of depression, panic, and somatic symptoms on illness behavior. Psychosom Med. 2005;67:596&#x02013;601. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16046373</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weich</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Donmall</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Somatic presentation of psychiatric morbidity in general practice</article-title><source>Br J Gen Pract</source><year>1995</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>143</fpage><lpage>147</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Weich S, Lewis G, Donmall R, Mann A. Somatic presentation of psychiatric morbidity in general practice. Br J Gen Pract. 1995;45:143&#x02013;7. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7772392</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rief</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Nanke</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Emmerich</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bender</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Zech</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Causal illness attributions in somatoform disorders&#x02014;associations with comorbidity and illness behavior</article-title><source>J Psychosom Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>367</fpage><lpage>371</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Rief W, Nanke A, Emmerich J, Bender A, Zech T. Causal illness attributions in somatoform disorders&#x02014;associations with comorbidity and illness behavior. J Psychosom Res. 2004;57:367&#x02013;71. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15518672</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rief</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Heitm&#x000fc;ller</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Reisberg</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>R&#x000fc;ddel</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Why reassurance fails in patients with unexplained symptoms&#x02014;an experimental investigation of remembered probabilities</article-title><source>PLoS Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>e269</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pmed.0030269</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Rief W, Heitm&#x000fc;ller AM, Reisberg K, R&#x000fc;ddel H. Why reassurance fails in patients with unexplained symptoms&#x02014;an experimental investigation of remembered probabilities. PLoS Med. 2006;3(8):e269. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16866576</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barsky</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Orav</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bates</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Somatization increases medical utilization and costs independent of psychiatric and medical morbidity</article-title><source>Arch Gen Psychiatry</source><year>2005</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>903</fpage><lpage>910</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/archpsyc.62.8.903</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Barsky AJ, Orav J, Bates DW. Somatization increases medical utilization and costs independent of psychiatric and medical morbidity. Arch Gen Psychiatry. 2005;62:903&#x02013;10. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16061768</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rief</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rauh</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Zech</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Bender</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of a general practitioners&#x02019; training: how to manage patients with unexplained physical symptoms</article-title><source>Psychosomatics</source><year>2006</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>304</fpage><lpage>311</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1176/appi.psy.47.4.304</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Rief W, Martin A, Rauh E, Zech T, Bender A. Evaluation of a general practitioners&#x02019; training: how to manage patients with unexplained physical symptoms. Psychosomatics. 2006;47:304&#x02013;11. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16844888</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="other"><bold>Salmon P, Peters S, Clifford R, et al.</bold> Why do general practitioners decline training to improve management of medically unexplained symptoms? DOI  http://10.1007/s11606-006-0094-z (in this issue).</citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>